{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>All the congregation, the wilderness of Zin.</b> A complete congregation, for the wilderness generation had already died, and now the children came to the land of Canaan in the first month, and it was the fortieth year. Know that there is nothing in the Torah at all — no event or any prophecy — except in the first year and in the fortieth year." "<b>And the people stayed in Kadesh.</b> Kadesh is the name of a city, and it is the wilderness of Zin, as it is written in the journeys in the section <i>Elle Mas'ei</i> (Numbers 33): ״ויחנו במדבר צן היא קדש״. And this is not Kadesh-barnea, for Kadesh-barnea is a wilderness, as it is written (Psalms 29): ״יחיל ה׳ מדבר קדש״. And the wilderness of Zin is not the wilderness of Sin written with a <i>samekh</i>, for that which is written with a <i>samekh</i> is a different wilderness between Elim and Sinai, as it is written (Exodus 16): ״ויסעו מאילם ויבאו וגו׳ אל מדבר סין אשר בין אילם ובין סיני״, and this shows that the wilderness of Sin with a <i>samekh</i> is a wilderness unto itself — it is not the wilderness of Zin written with a <i>tsadi</i>, nor is it the wilderness of Sinai, as it is written in <i>Elle Mas'ei</i> (Numbers 33): ״ויסעו מים סוף ויחנו במדבר סין״, and it is written (ibid.): ״ויסעו מרפידים ויחנו במדבר סיני״, and it counts no fewer than five journeys between the wilderness of Sin and the wilderness of Sinai." "<b>And know</b> that many days the children of Israel stayed in this city whose name is Kadesh, as it is written (Deuteronomy 1:46): ״ותשבו בקדש ימים רבים״. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: every place where it says וישב it means nothing but an expression of affliction, and therefore it is written ״ותמת שם מרים״, and immediately juxtaposed is the matter of the rock, which was the cause of the death of Moses and Aaron in the wilderness, and they did not merit to enter the land."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {1 "The citation תהלים כט for יחיל ה׳ מדבר קדש is problematic: this phrase does not appear in Psalm 29; it occurs in Psalm 29:8 as יחיל ה׳ מדבר קדש but some read the verse differently. Translated the citation as printed."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:11.960180365Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}